<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnulf, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/937">937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Arnulf the Bad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnulf, called the Bad, was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 907 to 937, the son of Margrave Luitpold, who had fallen against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a>. He defended Bavaria against Magyar raids and made it a powerful stem duchy, and in 919 some <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavarians">Bavarians</a> proclaimed him king before he submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a> in 921. His nickname came from monastic writers angered by his seizure of church lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arnulf-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Arnulf, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown / неизвестно · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arnulf_II._Pfalzgraf_von_Bayern.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
